1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:03,329
On this Records screen, Drafts
and Recent show different

2
00:00:03,329 --> 00:00:05,010
parts of an entry’s progress.

3
00:00:05,440 --> 00:00:08,739
Find the training entry in Drafts
and compare its descriptive

4
00:00:08,739 --> 00:00:10,010
text before opening it.

5
00:00:10,550 --> 00:00:14,090
The reference beginning with
D identifies this draft; it is

6
00:00:14,090 --> 00:00:15,920
not yet the final record number.

7
00:00:16,309 --> 00:00:20,030
Open that entry, keeping it distinct
from the separate Work draft.

8
00:00:20,239 --> 00:00:24,489
The opened form is Training Only,
Community software exercise.

9
00:00:24,890 --> 00:00:29,309
In Details, Summary is marked
required, and Notes provides space

10
00:00:29,309 --> 00:00:30,840
for the supporting explanation.

11
00:00:31,279 --> 00:00:34,699
Read the existing Summary first
so you can recognize this record

12
00:00:34,699 --> 00:00:36,010
when you return to the list.

13
00:00:36,379 --> 00:00:40,000
The Notes currently describe a
fictional Resgrid form exercise.

14
00:00:40,469 --> 00:00:44,940
Under Attachments, Take a photo,
Choose a photo and Choose a file

15
00:00:44,969 --> 00:00:49,299
are available, while No attachments
yet shows this example has none.

16
00:00:49,469 --> 00:00:54,050
Update Notes with the information that
belongs in this entry, then choose Save.

17
00:00:54,510 --> 00:00:57,809
Here, the revised Notes explain
that the department form was

18
00:00:57,809 --> 00:01:01,769
reviewed in Responder and that this
is a software practice exercise.

19
00:01:02,160 --> 00:01:05,560
The app returns Saved, and
the record still shows Draft.

20
00:01:05,880 --> 00:01:09,829
Keep the unchanged Summary and draft
reference in view so you can tell this

21
00:01:09,829 --> 00:01:11,739
revision belongs to the same record.

22
00:01:11,949 --> 00:01:15,920
When you reopen the same draft from
the Records list, read Notes again.

23
00:01:16,420 --> 00:01:20,140
The revised software exercise
text is retained here, rather than

24
00:01:20,170 --> 00:01:22,180
only sitting in an unsaved editor.

25
00:01:22,579 --> 00:01:25,869
No attachments yet remains
the actual attachment state.

26
00:01:26,249 --> 00:01:29,460
Before completing the record,
compare the saved content with

27
00:01:29,460 --> 00:01:31,190
the work you actually documented.

28
00:01:31,410 --> 00:01:35,640
Read the statement, I attest this
Record is complete and accurate.

29
00:01:35,999 --> 00:01:39,830
The checkbox is initially empty,
and Finalize is unavailable.

30
00:01:40,250 --> 00:01:44,509
Select the attestation only after
checking the record’s actual content.

31
00:01:44,889 --> 00:01:49,030
In this example, that content describes
a fictional software exercise.

32
00:01:49,429 --> 00:01:52,860
With the attestation selected,
Finalize becomes available.

33
00:01:53,019 --> 00:01:56,229
Choose Finalize once when this
record is ready to complete.

34
00:01:56,630 --> 00:02:00,760
The app returns Finalized and displays
a final record number at the top

35
00:02:00,849 --> 00:02:02,529
in place of the draft reference.

36
00:02:02,890 --> 00:02:06,999
Summary and Notes are now read-only,
and the attachment-picking actions

37
00:02:06,999 --> 00:02:08,680
are no longer offered in this view.

38
00:02:09,050 --> 00:02:11,970
This is the observed completion
of this record, rather than

39
00:02:11,970 --> 00:02:13,509
a submitted review request.

40
00:02:13,629 --> 00:02:16,379
Use Back to return to
the Records workspace.

41
00:02:16,800 --> 00:02:20,710
In Recent, find the same descriptive
text together with its final

42
00:02:20,710 --> 00:02:22,900
record number and Finalized status.

43
00:02:23,219 --> 00:02:26,620
The separate Work draft remains
in Drafts, while the entry you

44
00:02:26,620 --> 00:02:28,669
completed is no longer listed there.

45
00:02:28,939 --> 00:02:32,590
Reopen that Recent entry and
confirm its number, Finalized

46
00:02:32,590 --> 00:02:34,700
status, Summary and Notes.

47
00:02:35,070 --> 00:02:39,140
This fresh readback retains the
saved content, and Save, Submit

48
00:02:39,140 --> 00:02:42,449
for review and Finalize are
absent from the completed form.

49
00:02:43,050 --> 00:02:46,859
Use the same identity, save and
final-readback checks for forms

50
00:02:46,859 --> 00:02:50,380
used by community paramedicine and
mental health teams, search and

51
00:02:50,380 --> 00:02:55,189
rescue, security companies, wildland
contractors, industrial responders

52
00:02:55,279 --> 00:02:57,220
and fire or EMS departments.

53
00:02:57,609 --> 00:03:01,400
Choose the content appropriate to your
department, and verify each record’s

54
00:03:01,530 --> 00:03:03,359
